# Git hooks are executed by `sh`, and this repo is developed on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true — which would check these out with CRLF endings and leave
# `sh` reading a stray \r as part of the last argument on every line. Nothing
# else in the tree is pinned: the working copy stays CRLF on Windows and Git
# normalises to LF in the object store as before, which is why Prettier is
# configured with `endOfLine: "auto"` rather than the default "lf".
.husky/* text eol=lf
